    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0848" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.AD1/281b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-26T22:00:00-04:00">April 26, 1943—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2643. Your 2826, April 22.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d750-f1"/> Murphy has been
                    authorized, on the understanding that a delegation is being named jointly by the
                    High Command and the National Committee, to extend to the appropriate French
                    authorities the formal invitation to the food conference quoted in the
                    Department’s circular telegram of March 24, 9 p.m.<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d750-f2"/> and to assure the French authorities that the French
                    representatives will participate in the conference with the same status as
                    representatives of other countries. Admiral Stark may so inform the French
                    National Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
